# BUGS

An atomic in memory the GPU maps write-combining (an image that is not a storage image, the backend's own) raises GPU_CACHEABILITY_FAULT and does nothing. The Mali backend has no 64-bit atomics (`shaderAtomic64`), as it claims no 64-bit integers.
Separate minification and magnification filters (`samplerMinMagFilters`) are probed (loinnir-test's ResourceCases, which say what they read) but not claimed: they read right but for the pixels of the quads a diagonal crosses, and the whole suite has not run with them on.
`INDEX_BUFFER_SIZE` is given in bytes, and an index past it is not checked.
Once, a list of a pass and a copy (then the CPU's) between two timestamps took 101 ms of the GPU's time where the same list had taken 0.3 ms, and the cause is not known.
Its passes make their tiler memory (a heap context, a chunk of 1, 4 or 8 MiB, a geometry buffer) for each pass and let it go with it; a pass that fills the chunk would raise TILER_OOM, which nothing yet answers.
The Mali backend's steps run one after the other on the GPU, never two at once, even where they share nothing. Its transfer kernels move one unit an invocation and read their parameters for each, which is not the fastest a copy could go.
The Vulkan backend's heap has 4096 textures, 16 samplers and, where it has them, 1024 storage images.
It does not resolve a depth or stencil attachment, enable alpha to one, or import a handle (Venus has no import).
What a device behind Venus reports is what the host GPU reports of what Venus passes on, which may be less than the host GPU has.
A pipeline made by a backend that doesn't say what it draws into (`GPUPipeline.targets` nil) is not held to its pass by `validate`; the Mali backend refuses a draw into another format when it replays it.
A copy between formats of different classes that Vulkan would allow (a compressed format into an uncompressed one of the block's size) is `.invalid`.
On Mali there is one viewport: the GPU has one scissor box a draw that a primitive can't choose by its ViewportIndex (the scissor array its primitive flags name, as inferred, raised a fault in every form tried, and the flag changed nothing).
